# Unity-authored serialized text is written with LF endings by the editor on
# every save. With core.autocrlf=true (common on Windows) git would check these
# files out as CRLF, so every editor save flipped their EOL and `git status`
# reported phantom modifications on a fresh clone (P0.E1.T1 round-trip finding,
# 2026-10-06). Pinning eol=lf makes the worktree match what Unity writes, so
# open → edit → close leaves `git status` clean. All listed types verified
# text-only (0 NUL bytes across 274 tracked files).
*.unity          text eol=lf
*.prefab         text eol=lf
*.asset          text eol=lf
*.meta           text eol=lf
*.lighting       text eol=lf
*.mat            text eol=lf
*.anim           text eol=lf
*.controller     text eol=lf
*.shadergraph    text eol=lf
*.shadersubgraph text eol=lf
*.asmdef         text eol=lf
*.inputactions   text eol=lf
*.json           text eol=lf